names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lukanidin</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Mareel</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>van Roy</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>E-cadherin and metastasin (mts-1/S100A4) expression levels are inversely regulated in two tumor cell families</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1998</year><volume>58</volume><fpage>4587</fpage><lpage>4591</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||58|4587||bib14|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9788607</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kimura</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Endo</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Yonemura</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Heizmann</surname><given-names>CW</given-names></name><name><surname>Schafer</surname><given-names>BW</given-names></name><name><surname>Watanabe</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Sasaki</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical significance of S100A4 and E-cadherin-related adhesion molecules in non-small cell lung cancer</article-title><source>Int J Oncol</source><year>2000</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>1125</fpage><lpage>1131</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Oncol||16|1125||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10811984</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kriajevska</surname><given-names>MV</given-names></name><name><surname>Cardenas</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name><name><surname>Griorian</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Ambartsumian</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name><name><surname>Georgiev</surname><given-names>GP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lukani